WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.458 --> 00:00:11.480
I'm at the airport with my family.

2
00:00:12.741 --> 00:00:15.983
We're taking a trip to Vietnam to visit my grandparents.

3
00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:20.527
Vietnam is halfway around the world from here.

4
00:00:22.068 --> 00:00:24.931
That means it'll be a very long flight!

5
00:00:29.955 --> 00:00:31.116
Flying is fun.

6
00:00:32.444 --> 00:00:36.446
I like being up in the sky and looking down at the clouds.

7
00:00:37.847 --> 00:00:40.528
But do you know what I'd love to do one day?

8
00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:45.610
I want to look down at Earth—from outer space!

9
00:00:46.831 --> 00:00:51.993
And soon it could be possible because space travel is changing fast.

10
00:00:54.414 --> 00:00:57.716
For many years only astronauts traveled to space.

11
00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:05.643
But today, private companies are building spaceships so that others can visit space too.

12
00:01:09.465 --> 00:01:14.028
companies have created a whole new market called space tourism.

13
00:01:15.528 --> 00:01:19.811
Space tourists pay money to travel above Earth in spaceships.

14
00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:24.973
So far there are mainly two kinds of space tourism.

15
00:01:26.994 --> 00:01:29.696
Suborbital space tourists take short trips.

16
00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:36.292
People travel about 97 kilometers above Earth, to the edge of outer space.

17
00:01:37.713 --> 00:01:41.556
There's no gravity there, so they feel weightless for a few minutes.

18
00:01:42.837 --> 00:01:45.900
They also get an amazing view of Earth.

19
00:01:47.061 --> 00:01:52.345
They see its curved surface, outlined by the thin blue line of the atmosphere.

20
00:01:53.666 --> 00:01:55.788
Countless stars fill the background.

21
00:01:57.596 --> 00:02:01.460
A suborbital trip lasts between ten minutes and a couple of hours.

22
00:02:03.361 --> 00:02:10.708
Orbital space tourists go much higher, traveling about 320 kilometers above Earth.

23
00:02:12.229 --> 00:02:15.091
This is high enough to enter Earth's orbit.

24
00:02:16.393 --> 00:02:19.896
This is the zone where an object will orbit around Earth.

25
00:02:21.537 --> 00:02:24.440
Some tourists go around the planet a few times.

26
00:02:26.352 --> 00:02:30.414
Others visit the International Space Station or ISS.

27
00:02:31.494 --> 00:02:34.356
Orbital trips last a few days or longer.

28
00:02:36.497 --> 00:02:40.699
Private companies are also planning to build space hotels.

29
00:02:41.919 --> 00:02:45.421
These hotels will be like space stations that orbit Earth.

30
00:02:46.661 --> 00:02:51.744
It's so cool—people will be able to take vacations in space!

31
00:02:54.448 --> 00:02:58.089
Several countries have big plans for building in space too.

32
00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.470
Many want to build bases on the moon.

33
00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:05.291
People will live and work on the bases.

34
00:03:08.032 --> 00:03:11.633
And they can be used to help scientists explore deep space.

35
00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:17.355
For example, missions to Mars could be launched from moon bases.

36
00:03:18.595 --> 00:03:21.536
Someday there might be whole colonies on Mars.

37
00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:26.163
If that happens, lots of people will be visiting space!

38
00:03:27.944 --> 00:03:31.747
Space travel is exciting, but it's also dangerous.

39
00:03:33.008 --> 00:03:36.231
Equipment can break down, causing deadly accidents.

40
00:03:38.173 --> 00:03:41.155
And human bodies aren't used to being in space.

41
00:03:42.656 --> 00:03:46.519
Space has high levels of radiation that can cause diseases.

42
00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:54.744
Also, without gravity, human bones and muscles grow weaker.

43
00:03:54.784 --> 00:03:58.507
Right now space tourism is only for very rich people.

44
00:03:59.648 --> 00:04:04.352
A ticket for a suborbital flight costs hundreds of thousands of dollars.

45
00:04:05.833 --> 00:04:08.435
Orbital space tourism costs even more.

46
00:04:09.656 --> 00:04:16.241
In 2022, people who visited the ISS paid over $50 million each!

47
00:04:18.682 --> 00:04:20.544
I can't wait to see Vietnam.

48
00:04:21.688 --> 00:04:24.630
Someday I want to tour the moon too.

49
00:04:25.911 --> 00:04:27.893
After that, I'll travel to Mars.

50
00:04:29.334 --> 00:04:34.137
My space trips will be amazing—and expensive.

51
00:04:35.238 --> 00:04:37.200
I'd better start saving my money now!
